  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Find $x$ if $\\log_2(\\log_4 x)=\\log_4(\\log_2 x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=16$.\n\nChange both logarithms to base 2 and let $t=\\log_2 x$.",
      "worked": "The logarithms require $x>1$. Let $t=\\log_2 x$, so $t>0$ and $\\log_4 x=\\frac{t}{2}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right)&=\\frac{\\log_2 t}{2}\\\\\\log_2 t-1&=\\frac{\\log_2 t}{2}\\\\\\frac{\\log_2 t}{2}&=1\\\\\\log_2 t&=2\\\\t&=4\\\\\\log_2 x&=4\\\\x&=16\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck: $\\log_2(\\log_4 16)=\\log_2 2=1$ and $\\log_4(\\log_2 16)=\\log_4 4=1$. Hence $x=16$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
